"Thesis assumption","Red-team finding","Required correction"
"“Sovereignty” is a universal buying trigger","Most mid-market buyers do not budget for sovereignty as an independent category. They fund cyber risk, third-party risk, audit evidence, business continuity, insurance renewal, procurement, and AI approval.","Sell against an existing budget line; use sovereignty as a differentiator and board-level risk lens."
"A comprehensive dependency graph is the product","An enterprise-wide graph can become a six-month data-cleanup project that no buyer wants to sponsor.","Start with 3–5 critical business services and a bounded evidence model."
"Public-source intelligence can reveal operational truth","OSINT can verify vendors, exposure, corporate relationships, disclosures, breach signals, and regulatory change. It cannot prove internal architecture, data flows, recovery capability, or contractual rights.","Treat OSINT as corroboration and monitoring—not the source of truth."
"Data residency equals sovereignty","Residency is one factor. Control also involves legal jurisdiction, privileged access, encryption-key control, operational administration, contracts, portability, and recovery capacity.","Score control across multiple dimensions rather than assigning a simplistic “Canadian/non-Canadian” label."
"AI governance is a standalone software category","Inventory-only platforms are crowded and easily dismissed as paperwork.","Tie AI governance to real decisions: data handling, use-case approval, model/vendor exits, evidence retention, and control testing."
"Critical infrastructure should be first","It has severe pain, but procurement cycles, security reviews, references, and liability expectations are difficult for an early-stage advisory firm.","Build proof in regulated, high-trust mid-market organizations before targeting major critical-infrastructure operators."
"A dashboard proves resilience","A dashboard can report risk without improving recovery. Buyers will expose this weakness quickly.","Every material finding must connect to a named owner, tested control, remediation action, and recovery exercise."